    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> be the sample space associated to a random experiment. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfenced></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.&nbsp;Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8469;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math> is equal to"
